hypotheses.statement:
Let $H\subset\mathcal F$ be finite and ancestral. If $x,y\in X$ satisfy $x=P_Hx$ and $y=Q_Hy$, then $$\label{eq:paired}
 \frac{\|x+y\|+\|x-y\|}{2}
 \ge\sqrt{\|x\|^2+\|y\|^2/12}.$$ More generally, for all $s,t>0$, $$\label{eq:paired-two-parameters}
 \frac{\|x+ty\|+\|x-ty\|}{2}
 \ge\frac{\|x\|+st\|y\|}{\sqrt{1+12s^2}}.$$

Let $R>0$, $\varepsilon>0$, $x\in X$, and $(y_j)_{j\ge1}\subset X$ satisfy $$\|x\pm y_j\|\le R,\qquad\|y_i-y_j\|\ge\varepsilon>0
 \quad(i\ne j).$$ Then $$\label{eq:lens}
 R^2-\|x\|^2\ge\varepsilon^2/48.$$

