Let $1<p\le3/2$, $s=(p-1)/p$, and $f=sV^{-1/p}$, where $V$ is uniform on $(0,1)$. Let $Y_1,\dots,Y_n$ be independent variables, each distributed as the difference of two independent copies of $f$. For real scalars $a_1,\dots,a_n$, put $A=(\sum_{j=1}^n\lvert a_j\rvert^{p})^{1/p}$ and $Z=\sum_{j=1}^n a_jY_j$. Then $\mathbb Ef=1$ and $$\label{kw:heavy-bounds}
 \mathbb P(\lvert Z\rvert>u)\le10(sA/u)^p\quad(u>0),
 \qquad \mathbb E\lvert Z\rvert\ge A/54.$$
